---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import TierListFilter from '../components/TierListFilter';


import AdsterraBanner from '../components/AdsterraBanner.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Stand Out Tier List – Best Stands for PvP, Raids & Farming | Stand Out Wiki"
  description="Roblox STAND OUT tier list for November 2026. Ranked tiers for 1v1 PvP combat, Passione Train Raids, and Dalas farming speeds. Verified moveset analysis."
  canonicalPath="tier-list"
  breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Tier List' }]}
  schemaType="CollectionPage"
>
  <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-10 md:py-16">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mb-10">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1 rounded-full bg-rose-100 text-rose-800 text-xs font-bold mb-3 border border-rose-200">
        <span>Competitive Meta Analysis</span>
        <span>•</span>
        <span>November 2026 Season</span>
      </div>

      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl lg:text-5xl font-black text-slate-900 tracking-tight">
        Stand Out Tier List
      </h1>

      <p class="mt-3 text-sm sm:text-base text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
        Welcome to the definitive competitive tier list for Roblox <strong>STAND OUT</strong>. Rather than offering a generic, single-dimensional list, we rank every Stand across three distinct game loops: <strong>1v1 PvP Duels</strong>, <strong>Endgame Raids &amp; Boss Dungeons</strong>, and <strong>Dalas Cash Farming Speed</strong>.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Top Above-The-Fold Adsterra Native Banner -->
    <AdsterraBanner className="mb-10" />

    <!-- Interactive Tier List Component -->
    <div class="mb-16">
      <TierListFilter client:load />
    </div>

    <!-- Tier Criteria Explanations -->
    <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 p-8 shadow-sm space-y-6 mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-slate-900">Tier Ranking Criteria &amp; Methodology</h2>
      
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-6 text-xs text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
        <div class="p-5 rounded-xl bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200">
          <h3 class="font-extrabold text-sm text-rose-800 mb-2">PvP Combat Evaluation</h3>
          <p>
            PvP rankings prioritize frame data, combo confirm reliability from basic M1 light attacks, presence of unreactable guardbreaks, i-frame defensive tools (such as King Crimson Time Erase or Mandom Rewind), and Time Stop overwrite viability.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="p-5 rounded-xl bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200">
          <h3 class="font-extrabold text-sm text-emerald-800 mb-2">Raid &amp; PvE Evaluation</h3>
          <p>
            Raid viability is judged by multi-target sustained DPS against dense minion waves (such as 77 Rings graveyard mobs), super armor penetration, crowd disruption, and group survival utility (such as Mr. President sanctuary or November Rain crushing downpours).
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="p-5 rounded-xl bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200">
          <h3 class="font-extrabold text-sm text-amber-800 mb-2">Farming &amp; Economy Evaluation</h3>
          <p>
            Farming speed is determined by mob wipe efficiency for bounty loops, traversal velocity across town, and exclusive resource foraging passives like Shigechi's Harvest Search Party or lettuce dealer crop bonuses.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Editorial Deep-Dive: S-Tier & Meta Stand Analysis -->
    <section class="space-y-10 mb-14">
      <div class="border-b border-slate-200 pb-4">
        <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-black text-slate-900 tracking-tight">
          Current Meta Highlights &amp; S+ Stand Breakdown
        </h2>
        <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-600 mt-1">
          Detailed combat breakdown of the strongest Stands in STAND OUT right now and why they dominate the current meta.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
        <!-- SPTW -->
        <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-white border border-slate-200 shadow-xs space-y-3">
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
            <span class="px-2.5 py-0.5 rounded-md bg-rose-100 text-rose-800 text-xs font-black">Pinnacle Evolution</span>
            <span class="text-xs font-bold text-slate-400">Rank: S+ Overall</span>
          </div>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-black text-slate-900">
            <a href="/stands/star-platinum-the-world/" class="hover:text-purple-700 transition-colors">
              Star Platinum: The World (SPTW) &rarr;
            </a>
          </h3>
          <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
            Evolved from Star Platinum using an <strong>Opal Rokakaka</strong> at the Level 50 cap. SPTW remains the gold standard of high-impact burst. Its <em>Bane of Rats</em> catches projectile attacks, <em>Platinum Parry</em> negates aggressive rushes, and its 5-second <em>Time Stop</em> allows uninterruptible heavy beatdown strings that can eliminate over 70% of an opponent's health bar.
          </p>
          <div class="text-[11px] font-semibold text-purple-700 bg-purple-50 p-2.5 rounded-lg border border-purple-100">
            <strong>Key Matchup Advantage:</strong> Can move within frozen time against opposing The World users for up to 3 seconds.
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- King Crimson -->
        <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-white border border-slate-200 shadow-xs space-y-3">
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
            <span class="px-2.5 py-0.5 rounded-md bg-purple-100 text-purple-800 text-xs font-black">Pinnacle Stand</span>
            <span class="text-xs font-bold text-slate-400">Rank: S+ PvP</span>
          </div>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-black text-slate-900">
            <a href="/stands/king-crimson/" class="hover:text-purple-700 transition-colors">
              King Crimson &rarr;
            </a>
          </h3>
          <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
            The undisputed king of neutral bait and evasion. With <em>Epitaph</em> predicting and negating enemy strikes into an automatic counter-chop, and <em>Time Erase</em> granting total invulnerability and repositioning behind foes, King Crimson turns any enemy aggression into a lethal mistake. In Doppio mode, reduced footprint and swift throws enable deceptive guerrilla tactics.
          </p>
          <div class="text-[11px] font-semibold text-purple-700 bg-purple-50 p-2.5 rounded-lg border border-purple-100">
            <strong>Key Matchup Advantage:</strong> Time Erase completely ignores Time Stop if activated right before the freeze frame.
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- The World / TWAU -->
        <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-white border border-slate-200 shadow-xs space-y-3">
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
            <span class="px-2.5 py-0.5 rounded-md bg-amber-100 text-amber-800 text-xs font-black">Pinnacle &amp; AU</span>
            <span class="text-xs font-bold text-slate-400">Rank: S Tier</span>
          </div>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-black text-slate-900">
            <a href="/stands/the-world-alternative-universe/" class="hover:text-amber-700 transition-colors">
              The World: Alternative Universe (TWAU) &rarr;
            </a>
          </h3>
          <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
            Diego Brando's dimensional variant trades base The World's pure physical brawling for agile range pressure. Featuring revolving firearm shots, gasoline ignition zones, and razor wire tripwires, TWAU keeps brawlers at bay while maintaining a swift 3.5s Time Stop with rapid cooldown cycle.
          </p>
          <div class="text-[11px] font-semibold text-amber-800 bg-amber-50 p-2.5 rounded-lg border border-amber-100">
            <strong>Key Matchup Advantage:</strong> Dominates large open areas like Honolulu streets and gang territory wars.
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Kraft Work -->
        <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-white border border-slate-200 shadow-xs space-y-3">
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
            <span class="px-2.5 py-0.5 rounded-md bg-blue-100 text-blue-800 text-xs font-black">Epic Stand</span>
            <span class="text-xs font-bold text-slate-400">Rank: S Tier 1v1</span>
          </div>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-black text-slate-900">
            <a href="/stands/kraft-work/" class="hover:text-blue-700 transition-colors">
              Kraft Work &rarr;
            </a>
          </h3>
          <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
            Widely regarded as the strongest sleeper pick in STAND OUT. Kraft Work's kinetic energy manipulation locks enemies and incoming projectiles in mid-air. Stacking kinetic strikes onto frozen coins or pebbles creates an unreactable projectile barrage that shreds opposing block meters.
          </p>
          <div class="text-[11px] font-semibold text-blue-800 bg-blue-50 p-2.5 rounded-lg border border-blue-100">
            <strong>Key Matchup Advantage:</strong> Can freeze incoming knife volleys and bullets to completely neutralize ranged opponents.
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Best Stands by Game Loop -->
    <section class="bg-slate-50 rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 p-8 shadow-xs mb-14 space-y-6">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-slate-900">Best Stands by Activity in Stand Out</h2>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4 gap-4 text-xs">
        <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-white border border-slate-200">
          <div class="font-black text-sm text-rose-800 mb-2">Best for 1v1 PvP Duels</div>
          <ul class="space-y-1.5 text-slate-700">
            <li><strong>1. King Crimson:</strong> Supreme defensive i-frames.</li>
            <li><strong>2. SPTW:</strong> High-damage Time Stop punish.</li>
            <li><strong>3. Kraft Work:</strong> Kinetic lock lockdown.</li>
            <li><strong>4. Silver Chariot:</strong> Rapid armor-shed thrusts.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-white border border-slate-200">
          <div class="font-black text-sm text-emerald-800 mb-2">Best for Raids &amp; Bosses</div>
          <ul class="space-y-1.5 text-slate-700">
            <li><strong>1. Highway Star:</strong> Life-drain sustain &amp; rooms.</li>
            <li><strong>2. Magician's Red:</strong> High-density AOE burn.</li>
            <li><strong>3. November Rain:</strong> Crushing downpour stagger.</li>
            <li><strong>4. Star Platinum:</strong> Heavy boss super armor break.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-white border border-slate-200">
          <div class="font-black text-sm text-amber-800 mb-2">Best for Cash &amp; Farming</div>
          <ul class="space-y-1.5 text-slate-700">
            <li><strong>1. Harvest:</strong> Automated coin foraging passive.</li>
            <li><strong>2. Yellow Temperance:</strong> Tanky multi-mob clearing.</li>
            <li><strong>3. Bad Company:</strong> Autonomous squad DPS.</li>
            <li><strong>4. The Hand:</strong> Instant spatial swipe wipes.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-white border border-slate-200">
          <div class="font-black text-sm text-purple-800 mb-2">Best for Beginners (Starter)</div>
          <ul class="space-y-1.5 text-slate-700">
            <li><strong>1. Yellow Temperance:</strong> Natural physical shield.</li>
            <li><strong>2. Beach Boy:</strong> Safe long-distance hook grabs.</li>
            <li><strong>3. Sticky Fingers:</strong> Forgiving zipper mobility.</li>
            <li><strong>4. Magician's Red:</strong> Easy hitboxes and fire ticks.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Rarity vs Power Reality Check -->
    <section class="bg-white rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 p-8 shadow-xs mb-14 space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-slate-900">Rarity vs. Combat Strength in Stand Out</h2>
      <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
        A common misconception among newer players is that only Pinnacle and Mythical Stands are worth keeping. In STAND OUT, ability synergy, stat point allocation (up to the 150 SP cap), and Sub-Ability mastery (Hamon vs. Vampire) matter far more than summoning rarity alone.
      </p>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 pt-2 text-xs text-slate-700">
        <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200">
          <strong class="text-slate-900">Sub-Ability Multipliers:</strong>
          <p class="mt-1">
            Pairing an Epic or Legendary Stand with Hamon provides up to +20% physical damage and sunlight burn ticks, often out-damaging an un-mastered Pinnacle Stand with poor stat allocation.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200">
          <strong class="text-slate-900">Story-Locked Utility Stands:</strong>
          <p class="mt-1">
            Utility Stands like <em>Super Fly</em>, <em>Cinderella</em>, and <em>Burning Down the House</em> cannot be pulled from early arrows until completing the story, but offer irreplaceable utility for gang bases and cosmetic customization.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>
